{
  "_doc": "Forge Scribe — thresholds, caps and the deterministic NL+EN keyword classifier used by .claude/forge-bin/forge-scribe.cjs. Patterns are case-insensitive JavaScript regex sources. Each class sums the weights of its matching patterns; the highest class wins, a tie for the top or a zero score goes to 'unclassified' (never guess). Project data lives in .claude/forge-scribe/ and is never shipped.",
  "version": 1,
  "caps": {
    "digest_max_chars": 1200,
    "title_max_chars": 60,
    "_inbox_dedupe_doc": "Codex R3 SC-11: the same text is linked as a duplicate (duplicate_of, kept in the inbox, no second item) only within the SAME session and this short window; another session or a later repeat is a new prompt.",
    "inbox_dedupe_window_sec": 30,
    "_max_prompt_doc": "Codex R3 SC-09: the FULL prompt is redacted first, then capped at this length; a longer prompt is kept up to the cap and marked truncated with its original length.",
    "max_prompt_chars": 20000,
    "multi_ask_threshold": 3,
    "resume_dispatch_threshold": 20
  },
  "owner_check": {
    "_doc": "Codex R3 SC-01/SC-02: ack, cancel, a confirmed defer, a reclassification to question/ack/preference and a supersede without a live replacement need an owner prompt captured BY THE HOOK (source hook, session id, prompt id) in the hash-chained inbox, found as a typed message in ~/.claude/projects/<slug of this project>/ (the user profile from the OS account, realpath containment; no environment override), with an AFFIRMATIVE act bound to the R-id (or a batch phrase) in one sentence: the classifier reads that sentence as the intent and, after the intent's own words and the R-ids are removed, none of negation_words remains. Ambiguous never authorises.",
    "_transcript_match_doc": "WP-ACK-TEXT (2026-10-11): the owner often repeats the SAME words (acks, rule repeats) and a message typed mid-turn is logged as a queued_command under the running turn's prompt id, so prompt id + text can match several transcript entries. The entry whose delivery time is CLOSEST to the inbox capture time is used, and only within this many seconds either way; never simply the oldest.",
    "transcript_match_skew_sec": 120,
    "negation_words": ["not", "never", "no", "niet", "geen", "nooit", "nee"],
    "batch_ack_phrases": ["alles akkoord", "alles is akkoord", "alles goed", "all approved", "approve all", "all good", "everything looks good", "alles goedgekeurd"],
    "batch_cancel_phrases": ["schrap alles", "laat alles maar", "cancel all", "cancel everything", "drop everything"],
    "_binding_doc": "Codex R5 SV-01 (2026-10-10): the act must be bound to ONE item. A sentence that names the R-id (or holds a batch phrase) never authorises when it is a question (ends with '?' or opens with one of question_starts), holds any of conditional_words, or holds a clause WITHOUT an R-id that negates or matches conflict_words. Sentences are cut into clauses at , : dashes, parentheses and contrast_words (a contrast word inside the intent's own phrase, like 'laat ... maar', is not a cut); the clause naming the R-id must classify as the intent with no negation and no conflict word left. A clause that is only R-ids joins the nearest act clause through list separators only, never across a contrast word. A batch phrase never authorises in a sentence with a contrast cut (an exception). Literal words except conflict_words, which are regex sources.",
    "contrast_words": ["but", "however", "except", "excluding", "although", "though", "whereas", "while", "yet", "apart from", "other than", "only", "maar", "behalve", "echter", "hoewel", "terwijl", "doch", "alleen", "uitgezonderd", "behoudens"],
    "conditional_words": ["if", "unless", "once", "provided", "providing", "assuming", "when", "whenever", "as soon as", "after", "before", "until", "als", "indien", "mits", "tenzij", "zodra", "wanneer", "nadat", "voordat", "totdat", "mocht", "zo gauw", "op voorwaarde"],
    "conflict_words": ["pending", "remains?", "still", "later", "wait(?:ing)?", "on hold", "hold (?:it|off|on)", "blocked", "reject(?:ed)?", "declined?", "den(?:y|ied)", "reopen\\w*", "(?:keep|leave) [^.!?\\n]{0,30}open", "nog (?:niet|even|open|wachten|bekijken)", "staat (?:nog )?open", "blijf\\w*", "wacht\\w*", "openstaand\\w*", "afgekeurd", "afwijz\\w*", "weiger\\w*", "aanhoud\\w*", "heropen\\w*", "straks", "eerst nog", "tomorrow", "morgen", "next (?:week|time|sprint|month|release)", "volgende (?:week|keer|sprint|maand|release)", "eventually", "someday", "ooit", "binnenkort"],
    "question_starts": ["is", "are", "was", "were", "has", "have", "had", "did", "does", "do", "can", "could", "would", "should", "will", "shall", "may", "might", "must", "how", "why", "what", "which", "when", "where", "who", "kan", "kun", "kunt", "zou", "zal", "zijn", "heeft", "hebben", "mag", "moet", "wil", "wilt", "hoe", "waarom", "wat", "welke", "wanneer", "waar", "wie"],
    "_shared_list_doc": "WP-ACK-LIST (2026-10-11): an ack sentence made ONLY of two or more R-ids, list glue (, en and &), words from shared_ack_predicates and closing punctuation ('R-0006, R-0007, R-0016 en R-0012 kloppen.') authorises each id it names. Any other word (a negation, contrast, condition, deferral, 'tot en met') leaves residue and the one-item binding applies; a question mark never qualifies; ranges are never expanded. Literal words (multi-word allowed).",
    "shared_ack_predicates": ["klopt", "kloppen", "akkoord", "goed", "goedgekeurd", "bevestigd", "approved", "confirmed", "ok", "okay", "yes", "done", "is gedaan", "zijn gedaan"]
  },
  "repeat": {
    "_doc": "WP-SCRIBE-REPEAT (global CLAUDE.md 'Owner repeats = HARD RULE'): a captured owner prompt that repeats an earlier owner ask gets repeat_of + repeat_count; the hook, the digest and `list` show 'REPEAT x<n> of R-..'. Token sets only (forge-scribe-classify.cjs OWNER REPEATS): lower-case letter runs >= min_len, minus stopwords and cue words, light stemming (-en, -s), concept groups map synonyms to one weighted token. Match: weighted Jaccard >= jaccard (shared >= 2) OR shared >= min_shared OR containment >= containment (shared >= 2). A cue word/phrase in the new prompt adds cue_bonus. QUIET RULES (WP-REPEAT-FP 2026-10-11): a match needs >= 1 shared distinctive token (a concept token or a plain word >= distinctive_min_len letters; generic words are stopwords and never score); the cue bonus only counts once a distinctive token is shared (cue words alone never create a repeat); a pure status question (question form + a status_words word, no complaint_words cue, no imperative_starts start) is never flagged against a non-question earlier item unless it shares a weight-2 concept AND holds a complaint cue. Close the obligation with `forge-scribe.cjs transition R-n repeat-rule --ref standing_rule:<id>|decision_logged:<event_id> [--run id]`.",
    "enabled": true,
    "jaccard": 0.45,
    "min_shared": 3,
    "containment": 0.5,
    "cue_bonus": 1,
    "max_chars": 2000,
    "max_candidates": 400,
    "min_len": 3,
    "distinctive_min_len": 4,
    "status_words": ["nog", "open", "openstaand", "openstaande", "gedaan", "gebeuren", "doen", "status", "todo", "left", "remaining", "pending"],
    "imperative_starts": ["zet", "maak", "start", "voeg", "ruim", "doe", "bouw", "fix", "verander", "make", "add", "build", "run", "set"],
    "complaint_words": ["steeds", "weer", "nogmaals", "opnieuw", "alweer", "again", "herhalen", "herhaal"],
    "cue_words": ["steeds", "weer", "nogmaals", "opnieuw", "alweer", "again", "herhalen", "herhaal", "repeat", "repeating"],
    "cue_phrases": ["once more", "ik moet", "i keep", "i have to keep", "for the third time", "voor de derde keer", "zoals ik al zei", "as i said"],
    "stopwords": [
      "aan", "als", "alle", "alles", "alleen", "ben", "bij", "dan", "dat", "deze", "die", "dit", "doe", "doen", "door", "een", "elkaar", "en", "er", "geen", "het", "hebben", "heb", "hij", "hoe", "ook", "jij", "jou", "jouw", "kan", "kun", "kunnen", "kunt", "maar", "met", "mijn", "moet", "moeten", "mag", "naar", "niet", "nog", "nou", "omdat", "onze", "ons", "over", "per", "toe", "tot", "uit", "van", "veel", "voor", "wat", "wel", "wil", "willen", "wij", "zijn", "zal", "zou", "zodat", "zolang", "zoals", "meer", "maak", "maken", "zet", "zetten", "start", "starten", "gebruik", "gebruiken", "gebruikt", "leg", "uitleg", "gaan", "gaat", "graag", "even", "dingen", "ding", "iets", "alsjeblieft", "aub", "please", "voeg", "worden", "wordt", "hier", "daar", "dus", "want", "waarom", "welke", "ga", "gan",
      "vragen", "vraag", "vroeg", "mij", "open", "gedaan", "gebeuren", "gebeurd", "gebeurt",
      "the", "and", "for", "with", "that", "this", "these", "those", "also", "but", "not", "from", "into", "onto", "you", "your", "are", "was", "were", "can", "could", "should", "would", "will", "make", "use", "using", "add", "get", "let", "just", "all", "any", "some", "more", "than", "then", "there", "here", "what", "why", "how", "when", "which", "its", "our", "out", "now", "have", "has", "had", "does", "did", "don", "doesn", "thing", "things", "ask", "asked", "asking", "need", "needs", "question", "questions", "status"
    ],
    "concepts": [
      { "token": "parallel", "weight": 2, "words": ["lane", "lanes", "agent", "agents", "subagent", "subagents", "parallel", "parallelle", "parallele", "parralel", "parrallel", "paralel", "parallell", "parralell", "concurrent", "concurrently", "tegelijk", "tegelijkertijd"] },
      { "token": "watchdog", "weight": 2, "words": ["watchdog", "watchdogs", "waakhond", "waakhonden"] },
      { "token": "cleanup", "weight": 2, "words": ["opruimen", "ruim", "ruimen", "ruimt", "opgeruimd", "cleanup", "clean", "opschonen", "schoonmaken"] },
      { "token": "extra", "weight": 1, "words": ["extra", "additional", "additionele"] }
    ]
  },
  "impact": {
    "path_weight": 5,
    "word_weight": 1,
    "min_word_overlap": 2,
    "stopwords": ["de", "het", "een", "en", "van", "voor", "met", "dat", "die", "dit", "deze", "ook", "maar", "niet", "wel", "nog", "naar", "op", "in", "aan", "bij", "the", "and", "for", "with", "that", "this", "also", "but", "not", "from", "into", "onto", "please", "graag", "even", "moet", "moeten", "wil", "kunnen", "make", "should", "would", "could"]
  },
  "classifier": {
    "classes": ["new", "change", "cancel", "preference", "question", "ack"],
    "patterns": {
      "change": [
        { "re": "\\bverander\\w*", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bwijzig\\w*", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bpas\\b[^.!?\\n]{0,60}\\baan\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\baanpass\\w*", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bin plaats van\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bipv\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bmoet\\b[^.!?\\n]{0,60}\\bworden\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\bliever\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\bhernoem\\w*", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bvervang\\w*", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bgroter\\b|\\bkleiner\\b|\\bdonkerder\\b|\\blichter\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\bchange\\b|\\bchanged\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bmodify\\b|\\bmodified\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\binstead of\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bswitch\\b[^.!?\\n]{0,40}\\bto\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\brename\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\breplace\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bmake (?:it|the|them|this)\\b[^.!?\\n]{0,40}\\b(?:bigger|smaller|darker|lighter|green|red|blue|faster|slower|larger)\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bshould be\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\bupdate the\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "^\\s*(?:kan|kun|kunt|can|could|would)\\b", "w": 1 },
        { "re": "\\b(?:remove|verwijder\\w*)\\b|\\bhaal\\b[^.!?\\n]{0,40}\\bweg\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\b(?:fix|repareer|herstel)\\b", "w": 2 }
      ],
      "new": [
        { "re": "\\bvoeg\\b[^.!?\\n]{0,60}\\btoe\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\btoevoeg\\w*", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\book wil ik\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bmaak\\b[^.!?\\n]{0,20}\\book\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bmaak (?:een|nog een)\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\bbouw\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\bnieuwe?\\b", "w": 1 },
        { "re": "\\berbij\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\bextra\\b", "w": 1 },
        { "re": "\\bik wil (?:een|ook|graag een)\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\badd\\b|\\badding\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\balso (?:want|need|build|create|make)\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bcreate\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\bbuild\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\bimplement\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\binclude\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\bnew\\b", "w": 1 },
        { "re": "\\bi (?:want|need) (?:a|an)\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "^\\s*(?:kan|kun|kunt|can|could|would)\\b", "w": 1 },
        { "re": "\\bgraag ook\\b", "w": 3 }
      ],
      "cancel": [
        { "re": "\\blaat\\b[^.!?\\n]{0,40}\\bmaar\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bschrap\\w*", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bniet meer (?:nodig|doen|bouwen|maken)\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bhoeft niet\\b|\\bhoeft (?:niet )?meer\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bvergeet\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bannuleer\\w*", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bstop met\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bnever ?mind\\b", "w": 5 },
        { "re": "\\bcancel\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bscrap\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bforget (?:about )?(?:it|that|the)\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bdrop (?:the|that|it)\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\b(?:don't|dont|do not) need\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bno longer (?:need|want)\\w*", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bskip (?:the|that|it)\\b", "w": 3 }
      ],
      "preference": [
        { "re": "\\bvoortaan\\b", "w": 5 },
        { "re": "\\bin het vervolg\\b", "w": 5 },
        { "re": "\\bvan nu af\\b", "w": 5 },
        { "re": "\\baltijd\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bnooit\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bstandaard\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\bfrom now on\\b", "w": 5 },
        { "re": "\\bgoing forward\\b", "w": 5 },
        { "re": "\\bin (?:the )?future\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\balways\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bnever\\b(?! ?mind)", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bby default\\b", "w": 3 }
      ],
      "question": [
        { "re": "\\?\\s*$", "w": 1 },
        { "re": "^\\s*(?:hoe|waarom|wat|welke|wanneer|waar|wie)\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bkun je (?:uitleggen|vertellen)\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bklopt het\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "^\\s*(?:how|why|what|which|when|where|who)\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "^\\s*(?:is|are|does|do|did) (?:it|this|that|the|there|we|you)\\b[^.!\\n]*\\?", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\b(?:can you|could you) explain\\b", "w": 3 }
      ],
      "ack": [
        { "re": "\\bakkoord\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bklopt\\b", "w": 2 },
        { "re": "\\bgoed zo\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bziet er goed uit\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\bgoedgekeurd\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "^\\s*(?:prima|top|perfect|super|mooi)\\b", "w": 3 },
        { "re": "\\bapproved?\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\blooks good\\b", "w": 4 },
        { "re": "\\blgtm\\b", "w": 5 },
        { "re": "^\\s*(?:ok|okay|great|perfect|nice)\\b", "w": 3 },
